<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ONE SUBSCRIPTION = ONE VIEWPAGER2 PAGE, and after the redesign the page is the
  TRAFFIC RING (handoff README §5.2): 172dp across, a 6dp stroke, filled from the
  top (−90°) clockwise, with the used figure and its ceiling stacked in the middle.

  WHY THE PAGE IS ONLY THE RING NOW. §5 lays the tab out as one vertical spine —
  профиль → кольцо → тариф → кнопки → автопродление → управление — and only ONE of
  those bands is per-подписка in a way the eye should be able to swipe: the traffic.
  The name, the срок, the two buttons and the auto-renew row all belong to whichever
  подписка is on screen and are stated ONCE, in activity_account.xml, re-bound by
  AccountFragment.renderSelectedSub on every page change. Repeating «Пополнить» on
  each page would have offered the same account-level action N times.

  This replaces the card's old @layout/view_meter include. The meter is not gone —
  it is this: the ring binds the same four states the meter documented (under quota,
  over quota, unlimited, no data), from the same figures, in SubscriptionPagerAdapter.

  The ring is a determinate CircularProgressIndicator and not a custom View on
  purpose. M3's indicator already starts its sweep at the top and runs clockwise,
  already rounds its cap (trackCornerRadius = half the 6dp stroke), and already
  draws the unfilled remainder as a track — which is the second circle in the
  prototype's SVG. What it does NOT do is §5's «переход 500 мс»: its own progress
  animation runs on the library's clock, so the adapter drives the sweep with a
  ValueAnimator on @interpolator/ease_out_quart instead (§8 «ease-out-quart»).

  indicatorTrackGapSize is pinned to 0: Material ≥1.11 opens a gap between the
  indicator and the track by default, and §11 grabl 7 («кольцо с двумя полосками»)
  is precisely that defect — one arc, never a segmented one.

  No MaterialCardView: §5 floats the ring on the page. A card around it would put a
  hairline box round the one object on this tab that is supposed to read as weight.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <FrameLayout
        android:layout_width="172dp"
        android:layout_height="172dp"
        android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal">

        <com.google.android.material.progressindicator.CircularProgressIndicator
            android:id="@+id/ring_traffic"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center"
            android:indeterminate="false"
            android:max="1000"
            android:progress="1000"
            app:indicatorColor="?attr/colorPrimary"
            app:indicatorDirectionCircular="clockwise"
            app:indicatorInset="0dp"
            app:indicatorSize="172dp"
            app:indicatorTrackGapSize="0dp"
            app:trackColor="?attr/colorSurfaceContainerHighest"
            app:trackCornerRadius="3dp"
            app:trackThickness="6dp" />

        <!-- The two centre lines. gravity=center on the column and on each line so a
             long figure («999,9 ГБ») stays optically centred in the disc instead of
             hanging off its own start edge. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_gravity="center"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:paddingHorizontal="@dimen/space_20">

            <!-- §5: «Цифра 28sp/700, letter-spacing −0.02em, моноширинная (tnum)» —
                 TextAppearance.App.Numeric.Ring is that token (§8 «28/700 цифра
                 кольца»), tabular figures and the −0.02 tracking included. The
                 tracking used to be restated on this view because the token carried
                 −0.01 while values/styles.xml belonged to another wave; the token is
                 the design's number now and the override is gone with it. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_ring_value"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Numeric.Ring"
                tools:text="2,0 ТБ" />

            <!-- «без ограничений» / «из 5 ТБ». Two lines allowed: «Лимит исчерпан»
                 and «Нет данных» both fit on one, but the ceiling of a long unit
                 must be able to wrap rather than ellipsize inside the disc. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/tv_ring_caption"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/space_4"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:maxLines="2"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.App.Caption"
                tools:text="без ограничений" />
        </LinearLayout>
    </FrameLayout>
</FrameLayout>
